=== CROSS-BOOT (same modem firmware, 2 days apart, kernel changed) ===
  AP interval  : corpus 903.674618 s  live 903.675206 s  -> 0.65 ppm
  T (modem up) : corpus 902.267398 s  live 902.775332 s  -> 563 ppm
  R (recovery) : corpus 1.407219 s  live 0.899874 s  -> delta +0.507345 s

  The AP interval is a ~1 ppm physical constant across the two boots.
  The 'modem-uptime period' moves by 563 ppm -- it is exactly 903.675 - R.
  => Doc 149 s2 ('the period is MODEM uptime, not AP uptime') is INVERTED.
